  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Natural talent for opening and filling an aperture is graded on a four-step scale from A down to D. D grade sits at the bottom of that scale among youths who still open an aperture. Below it there is no cultivation talent at all: the Awakening Ceremony walk ends before ten steps, and the youth remains ordinary clan labor.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, the Awakening Ceremony measures talent by how far a fifteen-year-old walks into the moon orchid flower sea while Hope Gu enter the body. Fang Yuan states the bands used there: below ten steps means no cultivation talent, ten to twenty is D grade, twenty to thirty C grade, thirty to forty B grade, and forty to fifty A grade.",
      "chapters": [
        5
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "gu_hope_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Gu Yue session that opens the story, the flower sea returns a number of C and D grade talents among the youths who qualify, while about half the walkers show no talent.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D grade is therefore the lowest band that still produces a Gu Master, not a label for failure.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The grade governs how much of the aperture the primeval sea fills, and therefore how much essence the Gu Master holds and how fast that essence recovers.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy elder states that a D grade talent’s primeval sea takes up about two to three layers of the aperture, and that the highest promotion reachable is from rank one to rank two.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clan expectation talk earlier places a D grade youth raised for three years as a rank one senior Gu Master and the foundation of the family.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Academy fieldwork later treats D grade students as the weakest band in group hunts: even working together they take only a few wild-boar tusks compared with B and C grade peers.",
      "chapters": [
        77
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher grades hold more essence and recover it faster; primeval stones remain the outside tool for closing that gap.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Talent grades sit beside the aperture mechanics on aperture and primeval essence. The ceremony that produces the grade is on Awakening Ceremony. The full ladder is on Aptitude.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-d-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_aptitude",
        "sys_aperture_and_primeval_essence",
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    }
  ],
